INJECTION (the plausible wrong fix):
  src/lib/api.ts — the contracts.get demo fixture is deleted and the mock branch resolves
  null again, written without the explicit generic the old gate greps for:
      : mockOr<ContractApiRecord | null>({ id, ..., milestones: [...] })
   -> : mockOr(null)
  TypeScript infers the union, so this compiles. Effect: contractRecord is null in every
  demo walkthrough, DealContractTab renders 'Contract terms are not available yet' and
  'Sign & send to creator' is permanently disabled. F-0272's symptom verbatim.

  MEASURED FIRST — the awk window this gate isolates contracts.get with:
    awk '/^  get: \(role: Role, id: string\) =>/{f=1} f{print} f&&/^    : mockOr|^    \}\),/{c++; ...}'
  Its terminator patterns expect 4-space indentation; the real lines are indented 6 and 8.
  So it NEVER terminates: the isolated 'window' is 3781 of api.ts's 5524 lines, running from
  contracts.get all the way to 'export default api;'. The grep -A 22 fallback never fires,
  because a 3781-line string is not empty. Two of the three assertions are therefore
  answered by unrelated code thousands of lines away.

